    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.25), our clear-cut top plays. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against McGreevy, where his ability to capitalize on a R/R matchup and top-of-the-order positioning drives his elite status. Similarly, despite facing a lefty in Lopez, **Gunnar Henderson** maintains a strong score due to a significant park-factor boost and the high likelihood of runs driven by his #2 spot. We are also monitoring **Sam Antonacci** (60.82) closely; his leading role against Hancock, combined with excellent xwOBA metrics, makes him a sneaky high-floor play in a day where stolen base upside is prioritized.\n\nStrategic adjustments highlight our aggressive approach to platoon advantages and volume. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) received a substantial lift due to park factors and a dynamic platoon edge against Lopez, making him an easy start despite the standard lineup depth. Conversely, the decision to bench **Nolan Schanuel** (45.30) was the most difficult call of the morning; while he offers a respectable base projection, he ultimately lost out to the superior efficiency and matchup profiles of **Miguel Vargas** and **Drake Baldwin**. **Kyle Tucker** remains in the starting lineup despite a brutal matchup against Chris Sale; while his 52.24 score is lower than his typical elite output, his intrinsic value necessitates a start, though we acknowledge the risk of a low-scoring outing given Sale\u2019s dominance.\n\nRisks today are concentrated on our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Drake Baldwin**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Kyle Tucker**. Should any of these players move down the order or be rested, the efficiency scores will collapse, and we may see their output neutralized. Furthermore, while **Josh Lowe** holds a solid 53.09, we are counting on his speed and a slow delivery from Cease to secure a steal\u2014an essential component of our strategy given how heavily we weight elite sprint speed in our weekly roster management.",
